Title: "Natural Numbers"
Id: "acc9e650-ac98-4a0b-821a-5bc440a9388e"


Text: "The natural numbers are the numbers of counting: zero, one, two, and so
       on without end. This chapter builds them from the ground already laid."
Id: "3079172c-5778-44bd-9391-60ce0f0b12e7"


[\naturals]
Defines: Nb ::= (N, 0, S(n_))
abstractly:
specifies:
. N is \set
. 0 "in" N
. S is \function:on{N}:to{N}
expresses:
. forAll: n "in" N
  then: S(n) != 0
. forAll: m, n "in" N
  then: (.S(m) = S(n).) \.implies./ (.m = n.)
. forAll: A \:subset:/ N
  then:
  . if:
    . 0 "in" A
    . forAll: n "in" A
      then: S(n) "in" A
    then: A = N
Enables:
. capability: n_ "in" Nb :-> n_ is \natural
. view:
  as: S := N is \set
Documented:
. called: "the naturals"
. written: "\mathbb{N}"
Id: "502e2a50-cced-461a-bdcf-03e2221a598f"


[\natural]
Declares: n
Enables:
. capability: n_ + m_ :=> n_ \.natural.+./ m_
Documented:
. called: "natural"
Id: "6c240df6-c06d-4fc4-ab16-31fa5aebb4d7"


[n_ \.natural.+./ m_]
Defines: n_ + m_ is \binary.operation:on{\naturals}
expresses:
. piecewise:
  if: n_ = 0
  then: n_ + m_ := m_
  else:
  . let: k is \natural
    where: n_ = \naturals..S(k)
    then: n_ + m_ := \naturals..S(n_ \.natural.+./ k)
Documented:
. written: "n_? + m_?"
Id: "a8dda59b-29db-4ac2-8d70-e9010ccae3e7"


[\(inductive)::set]
Refines: I
satisfies:
. \empty.set "in"? I
. forAll: X is \set
  where: X "in"? I
  then: \set.successor:of{X} "in"? I
Documented:
. adjective: "inductive"
Id: "68ba43e9-1329-4103-819e-16e20e8e7c9f"


[\von.neumann.omega]
Defines: omega is \set
expresses:
. let:
  . (.A is \(inductive)::set.)[:1:]
  . X is \set
  then:
  . have: X "in"? omega
    iff:
    . X "in"? A
    . forAll: I is \(inductive)::set
      then: X "in"? I
Enables:
. capability: X_ "in" omega :-> X_ is \set
Documented:
. written: "\omega"
Justification:
. [1]
  have: A is \(inductive)::set
  by: \axiom.of.infinity
Id: "c13f4641-0ed5-4ad7-b309-8ec13b4c6b77"


[\von.neumann.S(n_)]
Defines: S(n_) is \function:on{\von.neumann.omega}:to{\von.neumann.omega}
expresses: S(n_) := \set.successor:of{n_}
Documented:
. written: "S(n_?)"
. called: "Von Neumann Successor"
Id: "431ccff0-c289-46a7-b739-211c8ae805b4"


[\von.neumann.naturals]
Realizes: Nb ::= (N, 0, S(n_)) := \naturals
specifies:
. N := \von.neumann.omega
. 0 := \empty.set
. S(n_) := \von.neumann.S(n_)
Documented:
. called: "Von Neumann Naturals"
Id: "23196d3d-7a1f-44a8-899c-3c39d65bb331"
